3. Fonts
===============================================================================

  crates/casual-slide-text/fonts/   copied unmodified from OpenCalc at b23c67c,
                                    which took them from the upstream releases
                                    named in that folder's README.md

  Roboto           Apache-2.0      Google (github.com/googlefonts/roboto-2)
  Caladea          Apache-2.0      Huerta Tipografia (github.com/huertatipografica/Caladea)
  Carlito          SIL OFL-1.1     The Carlito Project Authors (github.com/googlefonts/carlito)
  Liberation Sans, Serif, Mono
                   SIL OFL-1.1     Red Hat and Google (github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts),
                                   liberation-fonts-ttf-2.1.5

  crates/casual-slide-text/fonts/noto/   added here on 2026-11-09 (T2D1-04), from
                                    Google's official Noto releases, unhinted
                                    static faces, unmodified

  Noto Sans Arabic SIL OFL-1.1     The Noto Project Authors (github.com/notofonts/arabic),
                                   release NotoSansArabic-v2.013
  Noto Naskh Arabic
                   SIL OFL-1.1     The Noto Project Authors (github.com/notofonts/arabic),
                                   release NotoNaskhArabic-v2.021

The OFL texts ship unmodified beside the fonts, in
crates/casual-slide-text/fonts/LICENSES/. The OFL governs the font files only and
has no effect on the licence of this repository's code. The fonts are
redistributed unmodified, not sold on their own, and no Reserved Font Name is
used for a modified font. Each face is embedded in the built engine as bytes, so
a distributed binary carries them under these same terms.

  webapp/fonts/cjk/                 copied unmodified from OpenCalc at 59742cf
                                    (its webapp/fonts/cjk), on 2026-11-08 (T2D5-02)

  Noto Sans CJK    SIL OFL-1.1     Adobe, Reserved Font Name 'Source'
  Noto Serif CJK   SIL OFL-1.1     Google

These are WOFF2 slices, a few hundred characters each, subset from the Noto CJK
releases by OpenCalc; a subset is a modified font under the OFL, and keeps the
family name Noto, not the reserved name. They are not compiled in: a host loads
the slices a document needs. The OFL texts ship beside them, in
webapp/fonts/cjk/OFL-Noto-Sans-CJK.txt and OFL-Noto-Serif-CJK.txt.

